{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Patchset 2 pushed (change 2600). Remediation of LLM-Review -1 + Verified -1, plus the P0 escalation.\n\nVerified -1 was MINE, not a pre-existing flake: tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py::test_completeness_every_gate_step_is_guarded_or_marked. The Verified lane runs workflows from trusted main against an arbitrary patchset, so a base predating this change has no e2e-deps rule and a bare 'make e2e-deps' would have failed the step — turning this fix into a red vote on other people's changes. Now guarded with a 'make -n e2e-deps' probe. Worth recording the local/CI skew that hid it: the gate only considers git-TRACKED paths, so my local run passed while tests/e2e/_toolchain.py was still untracked and CI failed the moment it was committed.\n\nLLM-Review blocking finding (the collection hook had no oracle) is addressed by driving the REAL conftest through a nested pytest over a replica tree with stub node/npm. Coverage is mutation-checked: eight mutations, all killed. One test was found VACUOUS by that exercise — removing the _PROVISION_ATTEMPTED guard changed nothing observable, because pytest_collection_modifyitems fires once per session. The flag was dead mechanism, so it was deleted rather than papered over with a test; _PROVISION_ERROR alone carries every observable behaviour.\n\nAdvisory 1 was a real bug and is fixed: browser_runner never consulted the provisioning state, so a failed npm ci surfaced for bpmn_harness and not for it.\n\nEscalation lever (playwright): measured, and the wall-clock number is NOT usable from this host — paired cold runs gave 111.8s omit-optional vs 63.4s full, then 420.9s omit-optional, i.e. registry variance dominates; --offline with a warm cache is ~1s either way. The reliable measurements are counts and bytes: 15 -> 11 packages, 30M -> 12M node_modules (playwright 4.8M + playwright-core 12M = 56% of the tree). One correction to the escalation: the published playwright package has NO postinstall script, so there is no browser download in this path — the saving is package download/extract only. playwright is now an optionalDependency and a selection with no browser test installs with --omit=optional.\n\nNote for readers of the next Verified run: the CI-side pre-provisioning step CANNOT be exercised on this patchset, because the Verified lane runs the workflow from trusted main. Only the portable in-process half is under test here."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788493252784131001,"uuid":"4b391792-e319-470e-9495-cccde8074089"}